course: dictionary
lesson: 9892
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One small word can have many meanings, and take is a good example. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to choose. «Breakfast takes 20 minutes» uses takes to mean needs or uses up time.
explain: «It remembers 14 July 1789, when people in Paris took the Bastille, a prison fortress.» Here took means got control of something by force. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Take can mean to grab something and carry it off, as in «a small hole keeps out bigger birds that would take the eggs or chicks». The birds want to steal the eggs. Phrases like «take a photo», «take a test» and «take turns» use take to mean do or have.
fact: Take is a verb, and its forms are take, takes, took, taken and taking.
fact: «Takes» with a time means it needs that much time: «The walk takes 10 minutes» means the walk needs 10 minutes.
fact: Take can also be a noun: «my take on it» means your view or opinion.
fact: To take something without asking means to steal it.
fact: In maths and exams, take away can be written as subtract or deduct, so «take 4 from 10» means subtract 4 from 10.
exercise: «Breakfast takes 20 minutes, so he must get up by 7:00.» What does takes mean here? | It carries the breakfast to the table | It steals the breakfast | *It needs or uses up time | It gets hold of a spoon
exercise: «...a small hole keeps out bigger birds that would take the eggs or chicks.» What does take mean here? | To lay them | To count them | *To grab and carry them away
exercise: Ella asks, «What's your take?» What is she asking? | A test you must sit | *Your opinion | A bag for shopping
test: «It remembers 14 July 1789, when people in Paris took the Bastille.» What does took mean here? | Carried it to a new home | Ate a meal | *Got control of it by force | Dropped it on the floor
test: In an exam, which word can replace take away when you are doing maths? | *Deduct | Donate | Decorate | Dance
exam: In which sentence does take mean to do or have something? | The walk takes 10 minutes | Take the cup to the kitchen | *We will take a photo of the sunset
